+## Baseline Calculator
+
+`src/lib/engine/baseline.js` › `calculateBaseline(records, indicators, window, options)`.
+- **Standard deviation:** sample SD (divide by n − 1), the usual estimate of day-to-day spread.
+  This is the `s` in the Drift Cut-off formula; `n` is its `m`.
+- **Raw SD is returned.** The per-indicator minimum SD (Drift Cut-off) is applied later, in the
+  z-score step, so the stored baseline stays the true measured value.
+- **Missing data:** only finite numbers count. Missing, null, NaN, infinite or text values are
+  skipped and counted, never filled in.
+- **Too few readings:** fewer than `minReadings` (default 2, the mathematical minimum) gives
+  `insufficient_data` with no numbers. The team still needs to choose the real minimum
+  (e.g. 10 of the 15 in-flight days) and pass it in.
+- **In-flight window:** `IN_FLIGHT_WINDOW` = mission days 21–35. The pre-flight window is not
+  decided yet.
+- **Field names:** indicator fields are passed in by the caller; the mission-day field defaults
+  to `missionDay`. Both follow whatever the daily record (CHECKLIST §1) defines.
+
+Status:
+ACTIVE (minimum readings and pre-flight window still to decide)
