+- **Field names** (`indicators.js`): camelCase, e.g. `heartRate`, `bpSystolic`, `bpDiastolic`,
+  `glucose` (mg/dL), `temperature` (°C), `sleepHours`, `mood`, `reactionMedianMs`,
+  `reactionLapses`, `reactionFalseStarts`, `exerciseMinutes`, `symptoms` (list), `spo2`,
+  `radiationMsv`, `missionDay`. CHECKLIST §1 "Daily record defined" should confirm or rename.
+- **Drift-tracked indicators:** the core six plus sleep, mood, reaction median and lapses,
+  exercise and SpO₂. Not tracked: false starts (no worrying direction given), symptoms (not a
+  number) and radiation dose (it accumulates by design).
+- **Minimum spread `s` per indicator** (Drift Cut-off gives none): heart rate 2 bpm, systolic
+  3 mmHg, diastolic 2 mmHg, glucose 4 mg/dL, temperature 0.1 °C, sleep 0.25 h, mood 0.3,
+  reaction median 10 ms, lapses 0.5, exercise 5 min, SpO₂ 0.5 %. Tune after simulator runs.
+- **Pre-flight window:** mission days −30 to −1. **Minimum readings per baseline:** 10.
+- **"Expected adaptation"** (status not defined before): the 7-day average differs from the
+  PRE-FLIGHT baseline by z ≥ 3.5 in the worrying direction but is NOT drifting against the
+  in-flight baseline: "changed since Earth, stable in space". This gives the pre-flight
+  baseline its job. Before day 36 nothing can be "drifting", as the in-flight baseline
+  isn't complete.
+- **Alert escalation:** an alert starts on the first day with 2+ drifting groups and ends only
+  on a day WITH data that has fewer than 2. It escalates when 14 days have passed since it
+  started. Days without data neither start nor end an alert.
+- **Red-limit severities:** `red` (opens the red-limit screen, caps the score at 25),
+  `act` (source gives an action) and `watch`. Only verified values are used; the 5 gaps in
+  `docs/SOURCES.md` stay empty. Glucose readings are treated as fasting (morning).
+- **Reminders:** every measurement once per mission day; SpO₂ and radiation not reminded.
+- **Region table** (`regions.js`) follows the indicators listed in `docs/BODY_MAP.md`; it is
+  the proposal for that file's open "agreed with the logic owner" check.
+- **Scenario Lab effect sizes** are invented demo values, never to be shown as physiology.
+
+Interim check of the 3.5 cut-off (Drift Cut-off asks for a re-run on our own simulator):
+with the engine and the test-data generator in `src/lib/engine/testData.js`, 100 healthy
+180-day missions gave 1 false alert and 100 of 100 declining missions were caught (median
+day 101; decline from day 75). 68 of the 100 healthy missions had at least one "note" day,
+so the UI should present a note quietly. Re-run with the real mission simulator (§1).
